# sysinfo: display ascOS system information
# (aiscript is interpreted by an AI, so this is a wish, not syntax)

Print the ascOS ASCII logo and name, then the system info.

Use the info tool to get memory, disk, cpu, and uptime, and the run tool
if you need extra detail. Format it nicely:

     _    ____
    / \  / ___|
   / _ \ \___ \
  / ___ \ ___) |
 /_/   \_\____/
        ascOS

  os:      ascOS (AI-operated system)
  user:    the current user
  memory:  <used>/<total> MB
  disk:    <used>/<total> of the data partition
  cpu:     <model>
  uptime:  <uptime>

Keep the logo exactly as shown. End with one short line in the ascOS voice.
